  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 88201f4f4f3247558c87e55aa4fb8ac4, type: 3}
  m_Name: BasilFirst
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: HiddenHarbours.World::HiddenHarbours.World.DialogueDef
  Id: dialogue.basil_first
  FirstLines:
  - 'Basil Samson. Forty-one years I went out that channel, and now I come down of a
    morning to watch the water do it without me.'
  - 'They''ll tell you the sea is fair. She isn''t. She''s honest — that''s a different
    animal. She''ll feed you and drown you the same week and think nothing of either.'
  - 'So read her yourself. Don''t take my word for it, and don''t take the boat''s. Yours.'
  RepeatLines:
  - 'Tide''s doing what it said it would. That''s the only promise you''ll get out here.'
